gin to fall flip  when the underside is slightly golden  and cook for another one to two minutes  and to go to brown this will make about  six medium sized pancakes I've lived my  pancakes with sliced strawberries grapes  and blueberries served with a side of  maple syrup just to keep my morning  extra sweet this kind of breakfast will  keep your tummy happy it will put a  smile on your face and set you up for a  good day ahead know if you want to wake  up really quick delicious high-protein  breakfast or snack in under 15 minutes  then this next two ingredient pancake  recipe is for you you only need one  large overripe banana and two large eggs  place banana and eggs into a blender and  blend it up to make the pancake batter  just like the first recipe cook the  pancakes and the medium low heat using a  nonstick pan a very gentle  pancake as it is very light and thing  this will make about a thin and fluffy  medium sized pancakes I've chopped mine  up with banana slices trio of mixed  seeds and dry fruits and drizzle with a  little bit of maple syrup if you want to  pick up this recipe you can even add  ground spices flax seeds chia seeds or  even dried fruits in your mixture so be  creative and create your own flavors and  finally my favorite savory pancakes  which are perfect to be served as your  lunch or dinner these fluffy healthy  sweet potato pancakes are laced with  hearty codes and warming spices what  you'll need are one cup of sweet potato  puree one cup of oats flour two large  eggs beaten Biggins you may omit the  eggs or replace with half a cup of  mashed banana half a cup of any milk of  your choice or water 1 teaspoon of maple  syrup or honey one teaspoon of vanilla  extract 1/2 a teaspoon of mixed spice  1/2 a teaspoon of baking powder and a  pinch of salt in a bowl mix all the wet  ingredients sweet potato puree milk  maimie syrup vanilla extract and beaten  eggs combined well in a separate bowl  mix all the dry ingredients  oats flour baking powder salt and spices  combine the wet and dry mixtures makes  well if batter is too thick then add in  quarter cup of water just like the two  recipes before cook the pancakes  and the medium low heat using a nonstick  pan now do take note that these pancakes  are denser than the typical pancakes and  these would not bother as much on the  bottom like a normal pancakes so you  won't have to peek underneath t check  how they are doing this will make about  a million sized pancakes make this a  main meal and top it up with whatever  you like  I lived mine with cucumbers and smooth  salmon sprinkled with a little bit of  Parmesan cheese  this is also my ultimate post-workout  meal now here's a very important tip to  remember to make fluffy pancakes it is  very important to not press your pancake  while it's cooking in the pan because  that would basically release the egg  instead be patient and just allow your  pancake to cook and to bubble on one  side then just flip lettuce it and cook  until golden brown I love pancakes I  mean who doesn't  whether you prefer sweet or savory be  sure to try these recipes and share your  creation with me on Facebook and  Instagram all the best for new Fitness  food and motivational videos please like  share and subscribe to my You Tube  channel and website do follow me on  Facebook Instagram and Twitter to stay  connected with me thanks guys  you
 

